  "title": "Ben Simmons For CJ McCollum? Stephen A Smith Thinks So!",
  "htmlContent": "<!-- wp:image {\"id\":512111,\"sizeSlug\":\"large\",\"linkDestination\":\"none\"} -->\n<figure class=\"wp-block-image size-large\"><img src=\"http://landonbuford.com/wp-content/uploads/2021/06/e5d80355828b4370995b432f4ab674fa.jpg\" alt=\"\" class=\"wp-image-512111\"/><figcaption>Philadelphia 76ers' Ben Simmons plays during Game 7 in a second-round NBA basketball playoff series against the Atlanta Hawks, Sunday, June 20, 2021, in Philadelphia. (AP Photo/Matt Slocum)</figcaption></figure>\n<!-- /wp:image -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p>Last night Bally Sports Brandon 'Scoop B' Robinson presented a couple of trade destinations for Ben Simmons if the Sixers were ready to part ways with the three-time All-Star. </p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p>The first destination for  Ben Simmons next season could be the Portland Trailblazers.</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:embed {\"url\":\"https://twitter.com/ScoopB/status/1406821188505067520?s=20\",\"type\":\"rich\",\"providerNameSlug\":\"twitter\",\"responsive\":true,\"className\":\"\"} -->\n<figure class=\"wp-block-embed is-type-rich is-provider-twitter wp-block-embed-twitter\"><div class=\"wp-block-embed__wrapper\">\nhttps://twitter.com/ScoopB/status/1406821188505067520?s=20\n</div></figure>\n<!-- /wp:embed -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p>The couple of places were Minnesota and Denver. Well, Robinson was not too far off with the Simmons to Portland because Stephen A. Smith this morning on First Take mention a possible swap of CJ McCollum and Simmons. </p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:embed {\"url\":\"https://www.instagram.com/tv/CQZK-8sHefg/?utm_source=ig_web_copy_link\",\"type\":\"rich\",\"providerNameSlug\":\"instagram\",\"responsive\":true,\"className\":\"\"} -->\n<figure class=\"wp-block-embed is-type-rich is-provider-instagram wp-block-embed-instagram\"><div class=\"wp-block-embed__wrapper\">\nhttps://www.instagram.com/tv/CQZK-8sHefg/?utm_source=ig_web_copy_link\n</div></figure>\n<!-- /wp:embed -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p>\"Try to get yourself, someone like CJ McCollum bring him to Philly send Ben Simmons to Portland because with all the perimeter guys it will work,\" said Smith.</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p>Philly legend Charlie Mack would agrees and wants Simmons to see the Wizard of OZ, and out of the city of Brotherly Love. </p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p>“Ben Simmons gotta go. Ben Simmons gotta go to The Wizard Oz. You need some courage medicine Ben Simmons. You are afraid… You gotta go Ben Simmons,” <a href=\"https://landonbuford.com/2021/06/21/affiliate-of-sixers-owner-will-smith-wants-ben-simmons-gone/\">said Mack</a>.</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p>Simmons averaged 14.3 points, 7.2 rebounds, and 6.9 assists per game this season. <gwmw style=\"display:none;\"></p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->",
